e are very  powerful tools that we will enforce so  you're saying Iran will feel it  absolutely and the economy they're not  doing that great anyway it's not doing  very well  their currency has depreciated  substantially and as the president was  very clear he wants to support the  people of Iran there are a lot of people  there they can have a bright future but  their bright future doesn't include  nuclear weapons ballistic missiles and  state-sponsored terrorism  here is the Senate Minority Leader on  this deal you're making it harder to go  after Hezbollah you're making it harder  to go after Iranian activities that are  really dangerous and you're probably  making it harder to come to a North  Korea deal and the foreign president who  weighed in with a statement President  Obama is saying at the time when we are  all rooting for diplomacy with North  Korea to succeed walking away from jcpoa  risks losing a deal that accomplishes  with Iran the very outcome that we are  pursuing with the North Koreans on that  specific point on North Korea do you  think North Korea looks at this and  interprets anything with the kind of  pulling out of the Iran deal right the  president is determined to make sure  Americans are safe if the president  listened to all the professionals he  wouldn't have been tough on North Korea  we put very strong sanctions on North  Korea our maximum pressure campaign is a  major reason why they are negotiating  six months ago people said that the  president was being too tough on North  Korea now he's sitting down and he's  willing to negotiate so the president is  determined whether it's North Korea or  Iran to protect the American people and  the previous deal did not protect the  American people it would have been easy  for him to kick this down the road the  way people did with North Korea the  president not willing to do that  Secretary Pompeo is there tonight in  Pyongyang the president announcing that  is the hope that he comes back with the  three Americans that have been held  hostage there I think I think we all  hope he does and last thing you just  came back from China the the press  write-up of that trip was pretty gloomy  your take on where that trade  negotiation is going I mean it's not  easy stuff but you know these are also  complicated issues and the president has  been very clear going back to the  campaign in an office the trade deficit  is too big that China companies have the  ability to do business here our  companies don't have the same reciprocal  treatment now the good news is since  Mara laga when President Trump and  President Xi first spoke we agreed the  common objective was reduced the trade  deficit and make it reciprocal we  haven't made enough progress in the last  year we went over there I think our  delegation was very clear and going  through these issues we came back we  briefed to the president he's very  supportive of our position and I look  forward to the vice premier coming here  and continuing our negotiations the  president is determined that we will  have a more level in balanced fair and  free and reciprocal trading relationship  and that's our objective so you're  looking forward to round two I am indeed  mr. secretary we appreciate your time  good to see you thanks a lot

